{"track":"qudrat","num":"3.01","slug":"algebra-essentials","title":"Algebra Essentials","subtitle":"ClipSAT Printable Practice Suite (clipsat.org) • Topic 3.01 • 20 FRQs + 25 MCQs • Difficulty Progression • Cross-Lesson Synthesis","sections":[{"heading":"Part I — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Foundational Fluency (1–7)","questions":[{"q":"If $x=4$, evaluate $3x+7$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Evaluating expressions","answer":"$3(4)+7=12+7=19$.","explanation":"$3(4)+7=12+7=19$."},{"q":"If $a=5$ and $b=2$, evaluate $a^2-3b$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Evaluating expressions","answer":"$5^2-3(2)=25-6=19$.","explanation":"$5^2-3(2)=25-6=19$."},{"q":"If $x=-3$, evaluate $2x^2+5x$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Evaluating expressions","answer":"$2(-3)^2+5(-3)=2(9)-15=18-15=3$.","explanation":"$2(-3)^2+5(-3)=2(9)-15=18-15=3$."},{"q":"If $p=6$ and $q=-2$, evaluate $\\frac{p-q}{q+6}$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Evaluating expressions","answer":"$\\frac{6-(-2)}{-2+6}=\\frac{8}{4}=2$.","explanation":"$\\frac{6-(-2)}{-2+6}=\\frac{8}{4}=2$."},{"q":"Solve $2x+5=17$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving linear equations","answer":"$2x=12$, so $x=6$.","explanation":"$2x=12$, so $x=6$."},{"q":"Solve $5x-8=27$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving linear equations","answer":"$5x=35$, so $x=7$.","explanation":"$5x=35$, so $x=7$."},{"q":"Solve $3(x-4)=21$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving linear equations","answer":"$x-4=7$, so $x=11$.","explanation":"$x-4=7$, so $x=11$."}]},{"heading":"Part II — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Intermediate Multi-Step Application (8–14)","questions":[{"q":"Solve $\\frac{x}{4}+3=10$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving linear equations","answer":"$\\frac{x}{4}=7$, so $x=28$.","explanation":"$\\frac{x}{4}=7$, so $x=28$."},{"q":"Solve $7x+3=4x+18$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving linear equations","answer":"$7x-4x=18-3$, so $3x=15$, and $x=5$.","explanation":"$7x-4x=18-3$, so $3x=15$, and $x=5$."},{"q":"Expand $(x+3)(x+5)$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying","answer":"$x^2+(3+5)x+3\\times5=x^2+8x+15$.","explanation":"$x^2+(3+5)x+3\\times5=x^2+8x+15$."},{"q":"Expand $(x-4)(x+6)$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying","answer":"$x^2+(-4+6)x+(-4)(6)=x^2+2x-24$.","explanation":"$x^2+(-4+6)x+(-4)(6)=x^2+2x-24$."},{"q":"Expand $(2x+1)(x-3)$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying","answer":"$2x^2-6x+x-3=2x^2-5x-3$.","explanation":"$2x^2-6x+x-3=2x^2-5x-3$."},{"q":"Simplify $3(2x-5)-2(x-4)$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying","answer":"$6x-15-2x+8=4x-7$.","explanation":"$6x-15-2x+8=4x-7$."},{"q":"Factor $x^2+9x+20$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Factoring","answer":"Find two numbers with sum $9$ and product $20$: $4$ and $5$. $(x+4)(x+5)$.","explanation":"Find two numbers with sum $9$ and product $20$: $4$ and $5$. $(x+4)(x+5)$."}]},{"heading":"Part III — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Challenging & Cross-Lesson Synthesis (15–20)","questions":[{"q":"Factor $x^2-2x-15$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Factoring","cross_lesson":"4.01 Geometry & Measurement","answer":"Find two numbers with sum $-2$ and product $-15$: $-5$ and $3$. $(x-5)(x+3)$.","explanation":"Find two numbers with sum $-2$ and product $-15$: $-5$ and $3$. $(x-5)(x+3)$."},{"q":"Factor $x^2-49$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Factoring","cross_lesson":"5.01 Quantitative Comparisons","answer":"Difference of squares: $(x-7)(x+7)$.","explanation":"Difference of squares: $(x-7)(x+7)$."},{"q":"Factor $6x+15$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Factoring","cross_lesson":"6.01 Sequences & Patterns","answer":"Common factor $3$: $3(2x+5)$.","explanation":"Common factor $3$: $3(2x+5)$."},{"q":"Solve $x^2+5x+6=0$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving quadratic equations by factoring","cross_lesson":"7.01 Data Analysis & Probability","answer":"Factor: $(x+2)(x+3)=0$, so $x=-2$ or $x=-3$.","explanation":"Factor: $(x+2)(x+3)=0$, so $x=-2$ or $x=-3$."},{"q":"Solve $x^2-7x+12=0$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving quadratic equations by factoring","cross_lesson":"8.01 Word Problems & Reasoning","answer":"Factor: $(x-3)(x-4)=0$, so $x=3$ or $x=4$.","explanation":"Factor: $(x-3)(x-4)=0$, so $x=3$ or $x=4$."},{"q":"Solve $x^2-16=0$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving quadratic equations by factoring","cross_lesson":"1.01 Arithmetic & Number Sense","answer":"Difference of squares: $(x-4)(x+4)=0$, so $x=4$ or $x=-4$.","explanation":"Difference of squares: $(x-4)(x+4)=0$, so $x=4$ or $x=-4$."}]},{"heading":"Part IV — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Foundational Concept Mastery (21–28)","questions":[{"q":"The graph shows $y=x^2-49$. What are its roots (where the curve crosses the $x$-axis)?","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving quadratic equations","choices":["x = 7 only","x = 49","x = 7 or x = -7","x = -7 only"],"correct":2,"answer":"The curve crosses the $x$-axis at $x=-7$ and $x=7$, matching $x^2-49=0$.","explanation":"The curve crosses the $x$-axis at $x=-7$ and $x=7$, matching $x^2-49=0$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["x**2-49"],"xmin":-9,"xmax":9,"ymin":-55,"ymax":15,"width":230}},{"q":"The graph shows two lines. What is their point of intersection?","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Systems of two equations","choices":["(1, 4)","(0, 5)","(2, 3)","(3, 2)"],"correct":2,"answer":"The two lines $y=x+1$ and $y=-x+5$ cross where both are true: at $(2,3)$.","explanation":"The two lines $y=x+1$ and $y=-x+5$ cross where both are true: at $(2,3)$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["x+1","-x+5"],"xmin":-1,"xmax":6,"ymin":-2,"ymax":8,"width":230}},{"q":"The number line shows the solution set of an inequality. Which inequality matches?","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Inequalities","choices":["$x\\geq4$","$x\\leq4$","$x>4$","$x<4$"],"correct":3,"answer":"An open circle at $4$ with shading to the left means $x<4$.","explanation":"An open circle at $4$ with shading to the left means $x<4$.","figure":{"type":"numberline","min":0,"max":8,"marks":[{"x":4,"open":true,"label":"$4$"}],"shade":[0,4],"width":250}},{"q":"The graph shows a line. What is its slope?","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Reading function graphs","choices":["$\\frac{1}{2}$","$2$","$-2$","$-1$"],"correct":1,"answer":"The line rises $2$ for every $1$ across, e.g. from $(0,-1)$ to $(1,1)$: slope $=2$.","explanation":"The line rises $2$ for every $1$ across, e.g. from $(0,-1)$ to $(1,1)$: slope $=2$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["2*x-1"],"xmin":-2,"xmax":4,"ymin":-6,"ymax":8,"width":230}},{"q":"What is the $y$-intercept of the line shown?","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Reading function graphs","choices":["$4$","$0$","$-4$","$1$"],"correct":0,"answer":"The line crosses the $y$-axis at $(0,4)$.","explanation":"The line crosses the $y$-axis at $(0,4)$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["-x+4"],"xmin":-2,"xmax":6,"ymin":-3,"ymax":7,"width":230}},{"q":"What is the equation of the line shown?","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Reading function graphs","choices":["$y=3x+1$","$y=x+3$","$y=\\frac{1}{3}x$","$y=3x$"],"correct":3,"answer":"The line passes through the origin and $(1,3)$: slope $3$, no intercept, so $y=3x$.","explanation":"The line passes through the origin and $(1,3)$: slope $3$, no intercept, so $y=3x$.","figure":{"type":"numberline","range":[-5,7],"points":[{"x":-2,"label":"P"},{"x":4,"label":"Q"}]}},{"q":"Find the slope of the line through the two marked points.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Reading function graphs","choices":["$2$","$\\frac{1}{2}$","$-2$","$4$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Slope $=\\frac{6-2}{3-1}=\\frac{4}{2}=2$.","explanation":"Slope $=\\frac{6-2}{3-1}=\\frac{4}{2}=2$."},{"q":"The rectangle shown has area $A=lw=48$ and length $l=8$. Find the width $w$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Substitution into formulas","choices":["$8$","$6$","$384$","$40$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$48=8w\\Rightarrow w=6$.","explanation":"$48=8w\\Rightarrow w=6$."}]},{"heading":"Part V — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Intermediate Exam Application (29–37)","questions":[{"q":"The bar chart shows four students' test scores. Whose score is exactly 12 more than 70?","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Word problems","choices":["Student B","Student D","Student C","Student A"],"correct":2,"answer":"$70+12=82$, which is Student C's score.","explanation":"$70+12=82$, which is Student C's score.","figure":{"type":"bars","categories":["Student A","Student B","Student C","Student D"],"values":[70,75,82,90],"ylabel":"score","width":230}},{"q":"If $x=6$, evaluate $4x-9$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Evaluating expressions","choices":["$33$","$24$","$-15$","$15$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$4(6)-9=24-9=15$.","explanation":"$4(6)-9=24-9=15$."},{"q":"If $a=-2$ and $b=3$, evaluate $a^2+2ab$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Evaluating expressions","choices":["$-16$","$8$","$-4$","$-8$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$a^2=4$, $2ab=2(-2)(3)=-12$. $4+(-12)=-8$.","explanation":"$a^2=4$, $2ab=2(-2)(3)=-12$. $4+(-12)=-8$."},{"q":"If $x=5$ and $y=-1$, evaluate $(x+y)^2-xy$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Evaluating expressions","choices":["$16$","$11$","$21$","$-5$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$(x+y)^2=4^2=16$; $xy=-5$. $16-(-5)=21$.","explanation":"$(x+y)^2=4^2=16$; $xy=-5$. $16-(-5)=21$."},{"q":"If $p=3$, evaluate $2p^3-5p$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Evaluating expressions","choices":["$49$","$39$","$33$","$69$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$2(27)-15=54-15=39$.","explanation":"$2(27)-15=54-15=39$."},{"q":"Solve $4(x+2)=3x+15$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving linear equations","choices":["$x=1$","$x=23$","$x=-7$","$x=7$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$4x+8=3x+15\\Rightarrow x=7$.","explanation":"$4x+8=3x+15\\Rightarrow x=7$."},{"q":"Solve $\\frac{2x-1}{3}=5$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving linear equations","choices":["$x=4$","$x=7$","$x=16$","$x=8$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$2x-1=15\\Rightarrow 2x=16\\Rightarrow x=8$.","explanation":"$2x-1=15\\Rightarrow 2x=16\\Rightarrow x=8$."},{"q":"Solve $6-2x=3x-9$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving linear equations","choices":["$x=-3$","$x=3$","$x=15$","$x=1$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$15=5x\\Rightarrow x=3$.","explanation":"$15=5x\\Rightarrow x=3$."},{"q":"Expand $(x+7)^2$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying","choices":["$x^2+7x+49$","$x^2+14x+14$","$x^2+14x+49$","$x^2+49$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$(x+7)^2=x^2+2(7)x+49=x^2+14x+49$.","explanation":"$(x+7)^2=x^2+2(7)x+49=x^2+14x+49$."}]},{"heading":"Part VI — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Challenging & Cross-Lesson Synthesis (38–45)","questions":[{"q":"Expand $(x-5)^2$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying","choices":["$x^2+10x+25$","$x^2-5x+25$","$x^2-10x+25$","$x^2-25$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$(x-5)^2=x^2-10x+25$.","explanation":"$(x-5)^2=x^2-10x+25$.","cross_lesson":"7.01 Data Analysis & Probability"},{"q":"Expand $(3x-2)(3x+2)$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying","choices":["$9x^2+4$","$9x^2-12x-4$","$9x^2-4$","$6x^2-4$"],"correct":2,"answer":"Difference of squares: $(3x)^2-2^2=9x^2-4$.","explanation":"Difference of squares: $(3x)^2-2^2=9x^2-4$.","cross_lesson":"8.01 Word Problems & Reasoning"},{"q":"Simplify $2(x+3)-3(x-1)$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying","choices":["$5x+9$","$-x+9$","$x+9$","$-x+3$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$2x+6-3x+3=-x+9$.","explanation":"$2x+6-3x+3=-x+9$.","cross_lesson":"1.01 Arithmetic & Number Sense"},{"q":"Factor $3x^2+12x$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Factoring","choices":["$3(x^2+4x)$","$x(3x+12)$","$3x(x+12)$","$3x(x+4)$"],"correct":3,"answer":"GCF $=3x$: $3x^2+12x=3x(x+4)$.","explanation":"GCF $=3x$: $3x^2+12x=3x(x+4)$.","cross_lesson":"2.01 Ratios, Proportions & Percentages"},{"q":"Factor $x^2-11x+30$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Factoring","choices":["$(x-5)(x-6)$","$(x-2)(x-15)$","$(x+5)(x+6)$","$(x-3)(x-10)$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Need two numbers multiplying to $30$, adding to $-11$: $-5,-6$.","explanation":"Need two numbers multiplying to $30$, adding to $-11$: $-5,-6$.","cross_lesson":"4.01 Geometry & Measurement"},{"q":"Factor $x^2+3x-18$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Factoring","choices":["$(x+2)(x-9)$","$(x-6)(x+3)$","$(x+9)(x-2)$","$(x+6)(x-3)$"],"correct":3,"answer":"Need two numbers multiplying to $-18$, adding to $3$: $6,-3$.","explanation":"Need two numbers multiplying to $-18$, adding to $3$: $6,-3$.","cross_lesson":"5.01 Quantitative Comparisons"},{"q":"Solve $2x^2-8x=0$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving quadratic equations","choices":["x = 8","x = 2 or x = 4","x = 0 or x = 4","x = 0 or x = -4"],"correct":2,"answer":"$2x(x-4)=0\\Rightarrow x=0$ or $x=4$.","explanation":"$2x(x-4)=0\\Rightarrow x=0$ or $x=4$.","cross_lesson":"6.01 Sequences & Patterns"},{"q":"Solve the system: $x+2y=8$, $x-y=2$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Systems of two equations","choices":["x = 2, y = 3","x = 6, y = 1","x = 4, y = 2","x = 8, y = 0"],"correct":2,"answer":"Subtracting: $3y=6\\Rightarrow y=2$, then $x=4$.","explanation":"Subtracting: $3y=6\\Rightarrow y=2$, then $x=4$.","cross_lesson":"7.01 Data Analysis & Probability"}]}]}